   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Perspective Squeeze\n\nTwo lines of heavy type endlessly trade height while corner-pinned perspective bends the flat stack into receding planes.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 7.5 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A looping hold (an outro, a background title, a stream screen) needs constant, hypnotic typographic motion.\n- You want an editorial poster feel: heavy condensed type crushed and stretched like a print layout come alive.\n- Two short words can share the frame: both lines are forced to the same width.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You need an entrance or a reveal: the type is fully visible from the first frame; use kinetic-warp.\n- The copy must stay easily readable throughout: lines spend most of the loop crushed to a third of their height.\n- You only need the vertical stretch without the perspective bend.\n\nVariables:\n- upper_text (string): Upper line, default \"STUDIO\"\n- lower_text (string): Lower line, default \"BEST\"\n- fill (color): Fill, default \"#f2f2f2\"\n- upper_font (string): Upper font, default \"Anton, Impact, 'Arial Narrow', sans-serif\"\n- lower_font (string): Lower font, default \"Anton, Impact, 'Arial Narrow', sans-serif\"\n- line_gap (number, 0-200): Line gap, default 50\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Perspective Squeeze\n\n  Two lines of heavy type endlessly trade height while corner-pinned perspective bends the flat stack into receding planes.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/perspective-squeeze/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"perspective-squeeze\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"7.5\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"upper_text\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Upper line\", \"description\": \"Top line, set large.\", \"default\": \"STUDIO\"},\n    {\"id\": \"lower_text\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Lower line\", \"description\": \"Bottom line.\", \"default\": \"BEST\"},\n    {\"id\": \"fill\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Fill\", \"description\": \"Text color.\", \"default\": \"#f2f2f2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"upper_font\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Upper font\", \"description\": \"CSS font-family of the upper line. Anton is loaded.\", \"default\": \"Anton, Impact, &#39;Arial Narrow&#39;, sans-serif\"},\n    {\"id\": \"lower_font\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Lower font\", \"description\": \"CSS font-family of the lower line.\", \"default\": \"Anton, Impact, &#39;Arial Narrow&#39;, sans-serif\"},\n    {\"id\": \"line_gap\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Line gap\", \"description\": \"Gap between the two lines inside the block, in stage pixels (1920×1080 stage).\", \"default\": 50, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 200, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Perspective Squeeze</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Anton&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .ps-stage { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; width: 1920px; height: 1080px; transform-origin: 0 0; }\n        .ps-block { position: absolute; width: 990px; height: 546px; transform-origin: 0 0; }\n        .ps-block svg { display: block; overflow: hidden; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"perspective-squeeze\" data-duration=\"7.5\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"ps-clip\" class=\"clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"7.5\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div id=\"ps-stage\" class=\"ps-stage\">\n            <div id=\"ps-upper\" class=\"ps-block\" style=\"left:465px;top:41px\"><svg width=\"990\" height=\"546\" viewBox=\"0 0 990 546\"><text id=\"ps-upper-text\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></text></svg></div>\n            <div id=\"ps-lower\" class=\"ps-block\" style=\"left:465px;top:587px\"><svg width=\"990\" height=\"546\" viewBox=\"0 0 990 546\"><text id=\"ps-lower-text\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></text></svg></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/CustomEase.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, options, fallback) {\n              return options.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            function col(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              if (typeof value === \"boolean\") return value;\n              if (value === \"true\") return true;\n              if (value === \"false\") return false;\n              return fallback;\n            }\n            function fit(el, maxPx, size, ratio) {\n              // Shrink el's font size until its scrollWidth fits ratio of the frame width.\n              el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var max = Math.max(1, root.clientWidth * (ratio || 0.9));\n              if (el.scrollWidth > max) { size = Math.max(10, size * (max / el.scrollWidth)); el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\"; }\n              return size;\n            }\n            gsap.registerPlugin(CustomEase);\n            function ease(name, a, b, c, d) { return CustomEase.create(name, \"M0,0 C\" + a + \",\" + b + \" \" + c + \",\" + d + \" 1,1\"); }\n            function mulberry32(a) { return function () { a |= 0; a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0; var t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a); t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t; return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; }; }\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            var TOTAL = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"7.5\");\n            function ip(t, a, b, from, to, e) {\n              var p = b === a ? 1 : (t - a) / (b - a);\n              p = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, p));\n              if (e) p = e(p);\n              return from + (to - from) * p;\n            }\n            function hash01(seed) {\n              var h = 2166136261;\n              for (var i = 0; i < seed.length; i++) { h ^= seed.charCodeAt(i); h = Math.imul(h, 16777619); }\n              h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 13), 2246822519);\n              return ((h ^ (h >>> 16)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n            }\n            function hashRange(seed, lo, hi) { return lo + hash01(seed) * (hi - lo); }\n            // Snap a frame number down to a stop-motion pose.\n            function qf(frame, step) { return Math.floor(frame / step + 1e-6) * step; }\n            function kf(t, keys, vals, e) {\n              if (t <= keys[0]) return vals[0];\n              for (var i = 0; i < keys.length - 1; i++) if (t <= keys[i + 1]) return ip(t, keys[i], keys[i + 1], vals[i], vals[i + 1], e);\n              return vals[vals.length - 1];\n            }\n            // Per-frame drawing: a pure function of the timeline time, run from a tween's onUpdate.\n            function tick(draw) {\n              tl.to({}, { duration: TOTAL, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(tl.time()); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n            }\n            var cubOut = ease(\"cub-out\", 0.215, 0.61, 0.355, 1);\n            var cubIn = ease(\"cub-in\", 0.55, 0.055, 0.675, 0.19);\n            var cubInOut = ease(\"cub-io\", 0.645, 0.045, 0.355, 1);\n\n            var stage = document.getElementById(\"ps-stage\");\n            var fill = col(vars.fill, \"#f2f2f2\");\n            var gap = num(vars.line_gap, 50, 0, 200);\n            var BW = 990, BH = 546;\n            function setup(id, text, font, size) {\n              var el = document.getElementById(id);\n              el.textContent = text;\n              el.setAttribute(\"fill\", fill);\n              el.setAttribute(\"font-family\", font);\n              el.setAttribute(\"font-size\", size);\n              el.setAttribute(\"textLength\", BW);\n              el.setAttribute(\"lengthAdjust\", \"spacingAndGlyphs\");\n              return el;\n            }\n            var upT = setup(\"ps-upper-text\", str(vars.upper_text, \"STUDIO\"), str(vars.upper_font, \"Anton, Impact, sans-serif\"), 603);\n            var loT = setup(\"ps-lower-text\", str(vars.lower_text, \"BEST\"), str(vars.lower_font, \"Anton, Impact, sans-serif\"), 124);\n            var upD = document.getElementById(\"ps-upper\"), loD = document.getElementById(\"ps-lower\");\n            var rest = [[0, 0], [990, 0], [0, 546], [990, 546]];\n            var upMid = [[0, -326], [990, 0], [0, 546], [990, 546]];\n            var upEnd = [[0, 352], [990, -428], [460, 546], [990, 546]];\n            var loMid = [[0, 0], [990, 0], [0, 225], [990, 546]];\n            var loEnd = [[0, 0], [990, 0], [0, 897], [990, 116]];\n            function pin(src, dst) {\n              // Solve the 8x8 system for the homography that maps the four src corners onto dst.\n              var a = [], rhs = [], i, c, r;\n              for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\n                var x = src[i][0], y = src[i][1], u = dst[i][0], v = dst[i][1];\n                a.push([x, y, 1, 0, 0, 0, -u * x, -u * y]); rhs.push(u);\n                a.push([0, 0, 0, x, y, 1, -v * x, -v * y]); rhs.push(v);\n              }\n              for (var col2 = 0; col2 < 8; col2++) {\n                var p = col2;\n                for (r = col2 + 1; r < 8; r++) if (Math.abs(a[r][col2]) > Math.abs(a[p][col2])) p = r;\n                var tmp = a[col2]; a[col2] = a[p]; a[p] = tmp;\n                tmp = rhs[col2]; rhs[col2] = rhs[p]; rhs[p] = tmp;\n                var d = a[col2][col2];\n                if (Math.abs(d) < 1e-12) continue;\n                for (c = col2; c < 8; c++) a[col2][c] /= d;\n                rhs[col2] /= d;\n                for (r = 0; r < 8; r++) {\n                  if (r === col2) continue;\n                  var fct = a[r][col2];\n                  if (fct === 0) continue;\n                  for (c = col2; c < 8; c++) a[r][c] -= fct * a[col2][c];\n                  rhs[r] -= fct * rhs[col2];\n                }\n              }\n              return \"matrix3d(\" + [rhs[0], rhs[3], 0, rhs[6], rhs[1], rhs[4], 0, rhs[7], 0, 0, 1, 0, rhs[2], rhs[5], 0, 1].join(\",\") + \")\";\n            }\n            function lerpC(a, b, k) { return a.map(function (p, i) { return [p[0] + (b[i][0] - p[0]) * k, p[1] + (b[i][1] - p[1]) * k]; }); }\n            var squish = ease(\"ps-squish\", 0.6, 0, 0.4, 1);\n            var SK = [0, 60, 118, 161, 196, 225];\n            var lowerSY = [100, 384.8, 270, 330, 150, 100];\n            var upperSY = [100, 35.8, 64, 45, 110, 100];\n            function cornersAt(f, mid, end) {\n              if (f <= 0) return rest;\n              if (f >= 70) return end;\n              if (f <= 45) return lerpC(rest, mid, squish(f / 45));\n              return lerpC(mid, end, squish((f - 45) / 25));\n            }\n            var stageScale = Math.min(root.clientWidth / 1920, root.clientHeight / 1080);\n            stage.style.transform = \"translate(\" + (root.clientWidth - 1920 * stageScale) / 2 + \"px,\" + (root.clientHeight - 1080 * stageScale) / 2 + \"px) scale(\" + stageScale + \")\";\n            tick(function (t) {\n              var f = t * 30;\n              var us = kf(f, SK, upperSY, squish) / 100, ls = kf(f, SK, lowerSY, squish) / 100;\n              var uh = 603 * 0.65 * us, lh = 124 * 0.65 * ls;\n              var top = (BH - (uh + gap + lh)) / 2;\n              var ub = top + uh, lb = ub + gap + lh;\n              upT.setAttribute(\"y\", ub); upT.setAttribute(\"transform\", \"matrix(1,0,0,\" + us + \",0,\" + ub * (1 - us) + \")\");\n              loT.setAttribute(\"y\", lb); loT.setAttribute(\"transform\", \"matrix(1,0,0,\" + ls + \",0,\" + lb * (1 - ls) + \")\");\n              upD.style.transform = pin(rest, cornersAt(f, upMid, upEnd));\n              loD.style.transform = pin(rest, cornersAt(f, loMid, loEnd));\n            });\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"7.5\");\n            if (tl.duration() < total) tl.to({}, { duration: total - tl.duration() });\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[\"perspective-squeeze\"] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
